WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
Good morning John.

00:00:01.099 --> 00:00:03.509
A month and a half ago I got on a plane and
flew to Los Angeles, California.

00:00:03.509 --> 00:00:04.990
First stop off of the plane: In-N-Out Burger.

00:00:04.990 --> 00:00:06.589
My cashier was a fan of SciShow!

00:00:06.589 --> 00:00:10.870
Second stop: my hotel, where I was asked by
the check-in person whether or not I was there

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:11.870
to party.

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.180
Seeing no sign that I was here to party, I
assumed he was joking.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:18.630
So I said something to the effect of like
"Duh, what part of this package with the baggy

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:23.700
eyes and the nerd... thirty-four year old
dirty T-shirt-wearing guy makes you think

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.270
that I'm not 100% turning down for what?"

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:29.280
But it turned out he was not joking, because
he then told me twenty different parties that

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:35.100
were happening within a block and the dress
codes for those, which I had no way of achieving.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.429
Turned out I was not just in Los Angeles,
John; I was in Hollywood.

00:00:38.429 --> 00:00:40.899
Staying at the Roosevelt Hotel.

00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:46.519
Advertised on Google Maps as having a celeb-friendly
nightclub and pool.

00:00:46.519 --> 00:00:47.609
I don't know what that means.

00:00:47.609 --> 00:00:52.219
It was a secret why I was in LA, and that
annoyed me because so many interesting and

00:00:52.219 --> 00:00:55.329
weird things happened, and the whole point
of being a video blogger is that when weird

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:58.010
things happen to you, you get to share them.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:01.960
But now, I CAN share the reason I was in Los
Angeles.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:06.810
I was there as part of this thing where YouTube
is promoting YouTube channels.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:10.250
They were taking pictures and videos of me
an Michael Aranda and Caitlin Hofmeister for

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:15.310
the SciShow promotion, print advertisement
and television advertisement campaigns, which

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:18.759
are now a thing in the real world all over
the place: in Chicago, in Los Angeles, in

00:01:18.759 --> 00:01:22.680
New York, and on television, during the Walking
Dead premiere, during the Big Bang Theory,

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.689
during Late Night with Jimmy Fallon...

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:28.350
The Walking Dead premiere was viewed by seventeen
million people, and all the people that didn't

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.399
TiVo through the advertisements saw ME.

00:01:30.399 --> 00:01:31.399
What did they think?

00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:32.430
What did they think about?

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.680
Probably not much.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.690
Usually when you see an advertisement, you're
like uhhaouwjevba.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:40.390
Hopefully, I subconsciously influenced them
into thinking that science is still cool and

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:46.460
that they are still curious about the world,
no matter what zombie pandemic is on the way.

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:50.670
Here's the thing about Walking Dead zombies:
they've been dead forever, and they're not

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:56.170
eating anything; there's not enough humans
left to create fuel for them, but somehow

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:59.060
they are magically able to continue moving.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.479
What powers them - are they photosynthetic?!

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:04.180
Maybe they're somehow tapped into dark energy
and that's powering them.

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:07.141
If we could end the zombie apocalypse and
capture some of them and put them, like, in

00:02:07.141 --> 00:02:10.810
hamster wheels with like a brain on the other
side of the wheel and they could just climb

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.340
after it forever, it would be infinite free
power!

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:17.070
We could go from the zombie apocalypse to
a complete utopia!

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.070
I'm just sayin'!

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:22.470
Anyway, how I feel about being on TV and on
the side of buses and subway cars is that

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:23.470
I don't know how I feel.

00:02:23.470 --> 00:02:28.070
A big piece of me understands that this is
a big deal, and it searches the rest of the

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:32.680
me for thing that I'm feeling about it, and
it is unable to find a feeling.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.050
The disconnected for me thoughts are like:
is this good for SciShow?

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.830
And I hope it is because I think that more
SciShow is better for the world, because we

00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:43.600
really do need to be a more scientifically
literate society, and I think that SciShow

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:47.080
does a fairly good job of that as compared
to television science stuff.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.580
And then another piece of me is: are these
campaigns in general, it's more than just

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.240
SciShow, good for online video as a thing?

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.750
The goal of the campaign isn't about SciShow;
it's about making Youtube seem like a legitimate

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:03.890
place to spend your time as a viewer, and
as a legitimate place for advertisers to spend

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:04.890
their money.

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:09.890
It's about welcoming far more people and also
more money into this medium than has ever

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:10.890
been here before.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:15.680
And I'm a little ambivalent about that because
as the Youtube community becomes so big and

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:21.780
multifaceted that it breaks from that singular
Youtube community into plural Youtube communities,

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:29.070
Youtube, as a thing, is a little bit less
special if it's mainstream.

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:37.170
Which is why I'm so extremely happy that Vlogbrothers
is way too weird to ever be actually mainstream!

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:39.020
And we are dedicated to that!

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:45.370
We will not allow Vlogbrothers to be unweird
enough for it to be mainstream!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:46.960
THIS HAS TO BE WEIRD!

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.660
I just grabbed you right by the neck, there.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:55.530
THE PIZZA JOHN HAS TO HUMP THE PUPPY SIZED
ELEPHANT WHILE SWOODILYPOOPING IN AGLOE, NEW

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:56.530
YORK!

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.580
DEATH TO PENNIES, JOHN!

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:58.870
I'll see you on Tuesday.

